viewed as peacemaker and reformist by  his supporters ashraf ghani hoped to  rebuild afghanistan after years of war  as with many in his country conflict and  foreign invasion saw him spending most  of his young adult years abroad  in lebanon he studied political science  then anthropology in new york where he  became an economist at the world bank  he was in the united states during the  september 11 attacks in 2001  which turned him to politics  several months later he returned to  afghanistan after the u.s led invasion  and subsequent fall of the taliban  as finance minister he led an attempted  economic recovery carrying out extensive  reforms my country is dominated by drug  economy and a mafia  textbook economics does not work in my  context and i have very few  recommendations from anybody as to how  to put together a legal economy the  poverty of our knowledge must become the  first basis of moving forward ghani gave  up his u.s citizenship in 2009 to run  for president  in 2014 he was voted into office  but there were accusations of fraud  ghani wanted to reform afghanistan but  national dialogue and peace always faced  serious challenges  if we want to have rule of law the high  level officials who are involved in  corruption should be removed so we can  have a transparent judicial system  as the economy struggled and conflict  with the taliban continued ghani's  authority took a hit  he was shut out of talks between the  taliban and the u.s and qatar  in 2020 ghani was re-elected as  president his win again over shadow by  accusations of fraud his main rival  rejecting the result  after the u.s announces plans to pull  all its troops out of afghanistan by  september 11 this year  the fight for control in afghanistan  reached new heights  the president standing firm  brothers and sisters there is no deal  and no will to surrender there are two  choices either to live with dignity or  to live with insult  with the taliban reclaiming provinces at  a swift speed and scale gani blamed the  u.s for departing abruptly leaving  afghanistan's security to struggle and  disintegrate  at the funeral of the government's  assassinated top media official ghani  took a hard stance against the taliban  everyone should know that we are  standing in our place like a mountain  their ways will be broken because they  have no message other than evil they  fill coffins with young people and send  them like savages we stand for the  humanity life and dignity of afghanistan  speaking to parliament ghani said  afghanistan would be back under  government control within six months  but in the days that followed provincial  capitals continue to fall  the taliban's offensive has caused a  mass exodus among foreign government  workers and also afghanistan's middle  class who had the money to escape abroad  but among those less fortunate there's  mass displacement and soldiers have  surrendered  the u.n says the number of civilians  killed or wounded in just two months is  the highest recorded since 2009 raising  concerns of a humanitarian crisis  the speed and success of the taliban's  advance astonished ghani's government  and the western leaders that supported  him with little incentive for compromise  talks backed by the u.s and its allies  between the warring sides failed to  reach a potential peace deal  for gani only time will tell  but it is a result that will always  color his legacy with the prospect of  peace now looking like a catastrophic  failure for all those involved  chilean wolf al jazeera
 

